comments.body:
@penfever #10881 is ready for review. For the two pinned Qwen3.8-27B mini-swe-agent partitions, it:

- restores the "Solution Originality" section in the task message of every trace;
- drops the 8,614 resolved traces on a pinned exclusion list: the 4 leaks I confirmed by hand and the 8,610 traces with 8 or more guess turns. That is 17.3% of the successful traces and 31.1% of their assistant tokens.

The list is loaded from [`exclusions.jsonl`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Min-Li/marin-sft-data-audit/blob/5cc076cc822550f96287c861cf70c00c7ee8b4a6/open_swe/pinned_f967cba3/exclusions.jsonl) at a pinned revision, the same way #10839 loads its exclusion list, so no IDs are hardcoded. The other 11 Open-SWE partitions are unchanged. The PR body has the cutoff plot and a blind spot check of the traces above the cutoff.
